  "text": "Iqa‘ Sittatu ‘Ashar Masri 32/4 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Sittatu ‘Ashar Masri Iqa‘ Sittatu ‘Ashar Masri (\"sittatu ‘ashar\" means sixteen, \"masri\" means Egyptian) is a rare iqa‘ mostly used in the Muwashah vocal genre. It spans 8 measures of 4/4, bringing its time signature to 32/4. Muwashah Badat Min al-Khidri (khana) Ensemble Al-Kindi Les Croisades Sous Le Regard De l'Orient Part I - Maqam Bayati Muwashah Badat Min al-Khidri (khana) Ghada Shbeir Muwashahat Muwashah Badat Min al-Khidri (khana) Louis Hage and Aida Chalhoub Iqa‘ Sittatu ‘Ashar Masri 32/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
